  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.9.4 stable: configurable Wasm linear-memory ceiling, end-to-end (host + module declared max agree). New `WasmBackendOptions.MaxLinearMemoryPages` (default 16384 / 1 GiB, configurable up to 65536 / 4 GiB) is now plumbed BOTH host-side (`WebAssembly.Memory` `maximum`) AND kernel-module-side (`WasmModuleBuilder.ImportSharedMemory` declared max). Default consumers see byte-identical output vs 4.9.3. Verified end-to-end by SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML's DA3-Small at `MaxLinearMemoryPages=32768`: op 93 `memory.grow` past 16384 pages succeeds, model runs 2m 28s past the rc.1 instant-instantiate-reject point (Data, 2026-05-03). Stable rollup of 4.9.4-rc.1 + rc.2. Note: cached memory's maximum is fixed at instantiation; raising the option after the accelerator already reused the cached memory has no effect. See [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) for the full per-version history.",
